{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter and Sally Plan a Road Trip"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "At Franklin Park Zoo"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le15ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking and Giving Permission"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you ask for permission, it is important to be polite."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Can I please feed the animals now?</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter's Dad</span>: Of course, Peter!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use a modal like <span class=\"italic\">can, may, could</span> or <span class=\"italic\">would</span> to ask for permission.</p> You can also ask a Yes or No question like <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIs it OK if\u2026\u201d</span> or <span class=\"italic\">\u201cDo you mind\u2026\u201d</span></p> Here are some ways to ask for and give permission."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asking for Permission\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Giving Permission\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could I take a few days off next week?</p> Can I ask you something?</p> Would it be alright if I change projects?</p> Do you mind if someone take my shifts next week?</p> Is it OK if I leave early today?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Sure.</p> Perhaps.</p> Of course.</p> No problem.</p> I don't mind.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "distinctly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very clearly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I remember distinctly when I rode on a camel at the zoo."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about a zoo visit."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to kid"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make a joke or to say something and not mean it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I said you could feed the bear, but I was just kidding. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "camel"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a tall four-legged animal with a long neck and two humps"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can take a ride on a camel at the zoo."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "zookeeper"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who looks after the animals at the zoo"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The zookeeper said I shouldn't feed the bears."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bear"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a big furry four-legged animal that is very strong"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Bears like to eat salmon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cool"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "interesting or good"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The rhinos at the zoo look so cool."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go to the Franklin Park website."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find the map in English, and locate the 5 different animal areas. Write down the name and two animals from that area."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out what hours the zoo is opened on weekends and the price of tickets."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Organize your information in the table below. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 7 sentences with the information from the table."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the information from your sentences with your partner."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Zoo  Weekend Hours</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Ticket Prices</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adults: $\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Children: $\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Animal Area Name</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Animal #1</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Animal #2</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\"